  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-qftx-coupled-penrose-incidence-geometry": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nLet $S^4={X\\in\\mathbb R^5:|X|=1}$ have its unit round metric and the orientation which, on the stereographic chart $S^4\\setminus\\{\\infty\\}\\cong\\mathbb R^4$, is $dx_0\\wedge dx_1\\wedge dx_2\\wedge dx_3$. Put $z_1=x_0+ix_1$, $z_2=x_2+ix_3$, and $r^2=|z_1|^2+|z_2|^2$; in these coordinates the metric is $g=4(1+r^2)^{-2}\\sum_{\\mu=0}^3dx_\\mu^2$. Identify $\\mathbb H^2$ with $\\mathbb C^4$ using a right quaternionic structure $j$ with $j^2=-1$, put $Z=\\mathbb CP^3=\\mathbb P_{\\mathbb C}(\\mathbb H^2)$, and define $\\pi:Z\\to\\mathbb HP^1=S^4$ by $\\pi(\\ell)=\\ell+j\\ell$ for a complex line $\\ell\\subset\\mathbb H^2$. Its fibres are projective lines $L_x\\cong\\mathbb CP^1$. In homogeneous coordinates $[\\lambda_1:\\lambda_2:\\mu_1:\\mu_2]$, the fibre over finite $z=(z_1,z_2)$ is the line\n\n$$\\mu_1=z_1\\lambda_1-\\bar z_2\\lambda_2,\\qquad \\mu_2=z_2\\lambda_1+\\bar z_1\\lambda_2,$$\n\nand the fibre over infinity is $L_\\infty=\\{\\lambda_1=\\lambda_2=0\\}$. Give $Z$ the Fubini–Study metric induced by the standard Hermitian metric on $\\mathbb C^4$ and give $\\mathcal O_Z(-2)$ its induced Hermitian metric. On the incidence chart $\\lambda_1\\ne0$, set $t=\\lambda_2/\\lambda_1$, $\\mu_1/\\lambda_1=z_1-\\bar z_2t$, and $\\mu_2/\\lambda_1=z_2+\\bar z_1t$. The horizontal complex directions of type $(0,1)$ are spanned by\n\n$$H_1=\\partial_{\\bar z_1}-t\\partial_{z_2},\\qquad H_2=\\partial_{\\bar z_2}+t\\partial_{z_1};$$\n\nThey annihilate the displayed holomorphic coordinates. Together with $\\partial_{\\bar t}$ they form a direct local frame of $T^{0,1}Z$. Here $H_i$ are the constant-$t$ chart lifts; their projected complex alpha-plane is intrinsic, but this chart splitting is not asserted to be the global metric splitting. Globally let $V^{0,1}=\\ker(d\\pi)\\cap T^{0,1}Z$, and let $H^{0,1}$ be its Fubini–Study orthogonal complement. Its lifts project to the same alpha-planes and may differ from the displayed $H_i$ by vertical components. All global horizontal/vertical form decompositions use this orthogonal splitting; local computations may use the displayed constant-$t$ splitting after retaining the resulting frame and normalization factors. The second projective chart supplies the same alpha-plane at $t=\\infty$. The line bundle $\\mathcal O_Z(-1)$ is the tautological holomorphic line bundle and $\\mathcal O_Z(-2)=\\mathcal O_Z(-1)^{\\otimes2}$."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-coupled-penrose-positive-orientation-asd": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nAt a finite point of the positively oriented stereographic chart in the definition of the incidence geometry, let $A$ be a smooth connection and $F_A$ its curvature. For $t\\in\\mathbb C$, evaluate $F_A$ on $H_1=\\partial_{\\bar z_1}-t\\partial_{z_2}$ and $H_2=\\partial_{\\bar z_2}+t\\partial_{z_1}$. Then $F_A(H_1,H_2)=0$ for every $t\\in\\mathbb C$ if and only if the self-dual part $F_A^+=(F_A+*_gF_A)/2$ vanishes at that point. The same equivalence holds at the omitted projective value $t=\\infty$ by using the second incidence chart."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-coupled-penrose-round-sphere-curvature": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nFor the unit round metric on $S^4$ in the incidence definition, the scalar curvature in the convention $R=\\sum_{a,b=1}^{4}g(R(e_a,e_b)e_b,e_a)$ for an orthonormal frame is the constant $R=12$."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-coupled-penrose-fibre-dolbeault": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $L=\\mathbb CP^1$ and let $\\mathcal O_L(k)$ be the degree-$k$ holomorphic line bundle. For the smooth Dolbeault complexes on $L$, the cohomology groups satisfy\n\n$$H^{0,0}_{\\bar\\partial}(L,\\mathcal O_L(-1))=H^{0,1}_{\\bar\\partial}(L,\\mathcal O_L(-1))=H^{0,0}_{\\bar\\partial}(L,\\mathcal O_L(-2))=0,\\qquad H^{0,1}_{\\bar\\partial}(L,\\mathcal O_L(-2))\\cong\\mathbb C.$$\n\nThe canonical bundle is $K_L\\cong\\mathcal O_L(-2)$; the last group is one-dimensional, and the first three vanish."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-coupled-penrose-injective-edge": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nAssume full AC and the following analytic comparison: for $r\\in\\{0,1,2,3\\}$, every finite-rank holomorphic vector bundle $G$ on $X=\\mathbb P^r(\\mathbb C)$ has a canonical isomorphism $H^q(X,\\mathcal O(G))\\cong H^q_{\\bar\\partial}(X,G)$ for every $q\\ge0$, and for $G=\\mathcal O_X$ one has $H^0(X,\\mathcal O_X)=\\mathbb C$ and $H^q(X,\\mathcal O_X)=0$ for $q>0$. Let $E\\to S^4$ be a smooth finite-rank Hermitian bundle with smooth unitary connection $A$, and let $F$ be a holomorphic bundle on $Z=\\mathbb CP^3$ smoothly identified with $\\pi^*E$ so that its Dolbeault operator is the ordinary vertical Dolbeault operator and the connection-horizontal alpha-plane operator from the incidence definition. Fibrewise harmonic projection of a global Dolbeault representative defines a linear map\n\n$$\\mathcal P_A:H^1(Z,F\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))\\longrightarrow\\Gamma(S^4,E).$$\n\nEvery global closed representative $\\alpha$ has a unique decomposition $\\alpha=\\alpha_H+s\\sigma+\\bar\\partial_F\\gamma$, where $s=\\mathcal P_A[\\alpha]$, $\\alpha_H$ is horizontal, $\\sigma$ is the normalized fibre-harmonic generator, and the vertical correction $\\gamma$ is smooth and glues over the base. The map is well defined and injective. The comparison is supplied by the local analytic Dolbeault-resolution theorem; no algebraic-to-analytic comparison is assumed."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-coupled-penrose-operator-coefficient": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the conditional analytic comparison and the hypotheses of the injective-edge lemma, with $A$ a smooth unitary anti-self-dual connection. For a cohomology class $\\xi\\in H^1(Z,F\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))$, let $s=\\mathcal P_A(\\xi)$ be its fibre-harmonic image. The unique correction of $s\\sigma$ that removes the horizontal-vertical component of its Dolbeault differential has remaining component $(\\nabla_A^*\\nabla_A+2)s$ in a nonvanishing local frame. Consequently\n\n$$\\mathcal P_A\\bigl(H^1(Z,F\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))\\bigr)\\subseteq\\ker(\\nabla_A^*\\nabla_A+2).$$\n\nThe scalar term is $R/6$ for the specified unit round metric, where $R=12$."
    ],
    "thm-qftx-coupled-penrose-vanishing": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nAssume full AC. Let $S^4$ have the unit round metric and the positive stereographic orientation for $z_1=x_0+ix_1$, $z_2=x_2+ix_3$. Let $E\\to S^4$ be any smooth finite-rank Hermitian bundle with a smooth unitary anti-self-dual connection $A$. On $Z=\\mathbb CP^3$ use the incidence equations $\\mu_1=z_1\\lambda_1-\\bar z_2\\lambda_2$, $\\mu_2=z_2\\lambda_1+\\bar z_1\\lambda_2$, with infinity fibre $\\lambda_1=\\lambda_2=0$. Suppose $F$ is a holomorphic bundle smoothly identified with $\\pi^*E$ and its Dolbeault operator is the ordinary vertical derivative and the $A$-horizontal alpha-plane operator. Then\n\n$$H^1(Z,F\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))=H^1(Z,F^\\vee\\otimes\\mathcal O_Z(-2))=0.$$\n\nThis applies to arbitrary reducible and flat summands. It assumes no algebraic-to-analytic GAGA, monad, or inverse ADHM normal form as an independent premise."
    ],
    "ex-qftx-penrose-flat-summand-vanishing": [
      null
    ],
    "ex-qftx-penrose-global-injectivity-boundary": [
      null
    ]
  }
